Z||000004||JOHN PANEK||11-18-2001||11:09 AM||||Thanks for taking the time to research my problem. Popular opinion seems to be a faulty ground. I'll try what you suggested and let you know of my results.<P>John Panek<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rprevo:<BR><B> Behind the cluster is a green piece<BR>of plastic is has the contact wires in it.<BR>If memory serves correct the same 12 volts<BR>that feeds the speedo is the same one<BR>that feeds the Temp. Maybe that Green<BR>Plastic is damaged. Take the temp gage<BR>out of the cluster and look at the back<BR>of it you will see four leads the top lead<BR>should be ground and the other two that<BR>are across from each other should be the<BR>one for 12 volts and the other for the sender.<BR>At any rate when you know witch is witch<BR>you can bypass the cluster and hook the gage<BR>up to the battery direct and the temp sender<BR>direct right at the back of the gage. I went through this last winter when<BR>I put a Gt Package in my SE. You need a Haynes or a GM Manuel, I used a Haynes.<BR>It was pretty accurate for wire colors.<P> Well Good Luck!<P>  rprevo@ameritech.net<P>[This message has been edited by rprevo (edited 11-17-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
